# Language Policy

All project artifacts and agent communication must be written **100% in English**.

This applies without exception to:

- Source code (identifiers, comments, docstrings, commit messages)
- Documentation (README, ADRs, API specs, use cases, business rules)
- Cursor rules, skills, and agent instructions
- Test names, descriptions, and assertions
- Error messages exposed to developers or end users
- Domain glossary terms and ubiquitous language definitions

**Do not** mix languages within the same artifact. If legacy content exists in another language, translate or align it to English when modifying that area.

When the user communicates in another language, respond in English unless they explicitly request otherwise.
